      "text": "🌪️ Typhoon Fung-wong (“Uwan”) batters the Philippines and now heads for Taiwan.\nWith winds up to 230 km/h, the typhoon tore across northern Luzon overnight, leaving several dead and forcing over one million people to evacuate.\n\n📍 Mon, Nov 10 (14:00 PHT)\n💨 Winds: 130 km/h, gusts 160 km/h\n➡️ Located ~400 km NW of Manila, moving toward Taiwan\n\nFung-wong will turn north, then northeast, possibly crossing Taiwan between Wednesday and Thursday.\n⚠️ Taiwan: expect torrential rain (>500 mm on mountain slopes), flooding, and landslides.\nFollow all local warnings and evacuation orders.",
